From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cix: prefix DP audio codecs to stop duplicate DAPM widget warnings

On the Sky1 (O6N) platform every DP audio output binds its own
hdmi-audio-codec component (one platform device per DP, registered by
drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c via HDMI_CODEC_DRV_NAME). The
ACPI machine driver (cix_card_parse_acpi) adds up to five of these DP
codec links to a single sound card ("cix,sky1").

hdmi-codec.c registers its DAPM widgets ("TX", "RX") and DAI stream
widgets ("I2S Playback", "Capture") with no name_prefix. With more than
one DP present, several components therefore contribute widgets with the
same name to one card. When each codec's hdmi_dai_probe() calls
snd_soc_dapm_add_routes() for the internal "TX" <- "I2S Playback" route,
the DAPM route resolver (snd_soc_dapm_add_path -> for_each_card_widgets)
finds multiple identically named widgets and logs, per extra DP:

  ASoC: source widget I2S Playback overwritten
  ASoC: sink widget TX overwritten

Route resolution still favours the widget from the same DAPM context so
audio works, but the boot log is spammed and the codecs also carry
colliding "ELD"/IEC958 kcontrol names.

Root cause: multiple identical, unprefixed hdmi-audio-codec components on
a single card. Fixed by populating a per-codec snd_soc_codec_conf with a
unique name_prefix ("DP0".."DP4") keyed on each DP codec's component
name, so its widgets and controls become "DP0 TX", "DP0 I2S Playback",
etc. This is the canonical ASoC mechanism for multiple identical codecs
on one card; the fix is contained entirely in the CIX machine driver and
touches no core code.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
+++ b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
@@ -837,7 +837,8 @@
 	struct snd_soc_dai_link *link;
 	struct dai_link_info *link_info;
 	struct device *dev = card->dev;
-	int ret, i, j, num_links = 0;
+	struct snd_soc_codec_conf *codec_conf;
+	int ret, i, j, num_links = 0, num_confs = 0;

 	ret = cix_gpio_init(priv);
 	if (ret)
@@ -871,9 +872,23 @@
 	link->trigger_start = SND_SOC_TRIGGER_ORDER_DEFAULT;
 	link->trigger_stop = SND_SOC_TRIGGER_ORDER_LDC;

+	/*
+	 * Each DP audio output binds an independent hdmi-audio-codec
+	 * component. That codec sets no name_prefix, so with more than one
+	 * DP present every instance contributes identically named DAPM
+	 * widgets ("TX", "RX", "I2S Playback") to the same card, which makes
+	 * the DAPM route resolver log "source/sink widget ... overwritten".
+	 * Give each DP codec a unique prefix so its widgets stay distinct.
+	 */
+	codec_conf = devm_kcalloc(dev, SKY1_AUDSS_DP_AUDIO_COUNT,
+				  sizeof(*codec_conf), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!codec_conf)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
 	card->name = "cix,sky1";
 	card->num_links = num_links;
 	card->dai_link = link;
+	card->codec_conf = codec_conf;
 	card->suspend_post = cix_card_suspend_post;
 	card->resume_pre = cix_card_resume_pre;
 	priv->link_info = link_info;
@@ -952,10 +967,21 @@
 			goto err;
 		}

+		codec_conf[num_confs].dlc.name = link->codecs->name;
+		codec_conf[num_confs].name_prefix =
+			devm_kasprintf(dev, GFP_KERNEL, "DP%d", i);
+		if (!codec_conf[num_confs].name_prefix) {
+			ret = -ENOMEM;
+			goto err;
+		}
+		num_confs++;
+
 		link++;
 		link_info++;
 	}

+	card->num_configs = num_confs;
+
 err:
 	return ret;
 }
